<article class="env-lemma" id="037D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037D">Lemma <span data-tag="037D">10.37.17</span>.</a> Let $(R_ i, \varphi _{ii'})$ be a directed system (Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/00D4" data-tag="00D4">10.8.1</a>) of rings. If each $R_ i$ is a normal ring so is $R = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i R_ i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak p \subset R$ be a prime ideal. Set $\mathfrak p_ i = R_ i \cap \mathfrak p$ (usual abuse of notation). Then we see that $R_{\mathfrak p} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i (R_ i)_{\mathfrak p_ i}$. Since each $(R_ i)_{\mathfrak p_ i}$ is a normal domain we reduce to proving the statement of the lemma for normal domains. If $a, b \in R$ and $a/b$ satisfies a monic polynomial $P(T) \in R[T]$, then we can find a (sufficiently large) $i \in I$ such that $a, b$ come from objects $a_ i, b_ i$ over $R_ i$, $P$ comes from a monic polynomial $P_ i\in R_ i[T]$ and $P_ i(a_ i/b_ i)=0$. Since $R_ i$ is normal we see $a_ i/b_ i \in R_ i$ and hence also $a/b \in R$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>